# Same syntax as .gitignore.
#
# Prettier only formats what it has a parser for: Markdown, YAML, JSON, HTML,
# CSS and JavaScript. Rust, TOML and extensionless files such as LICENSE are
# skipped automatically, and node_modules and .git are ignored without being
# told. None of that needs listing here.
#
# What is left is the case that actually matters: files Prettier *can* format
# and must not.

# Build output. `cargo doc` writes HTML, CSS and JavaScript into target/doc, and
# Prettier will cheerfully reformat several thousand generated files if allowed
# anywhere near them. This is the entry that earns this file its place.
/target

# `cargo vendor` output. Vendored source is not ours to reformat, and doing so
# produces a diff large enough to hide the one line that mattered.
/vendor

# --- Add below, with a reason ------------------------------------------------
#
# Generated changelogs -- uncomment if you adopt release-plz or cargo-release,
# which rewrite this file from commit messages:
# CHANGELOG.md
#
# Fixtures whose exact formatting is the thing under test -- trybuild UI tests,
# insta snapshots, golden files for a renderer:
# crates/*/tests/ui/
# **/snapshots/
